    "summary": "Large box-shaped carved dish of alder, roughly rectangular shape, curved ends, concave sides, curved profile to the bowl, broad rim, inlaid with opercula, none missing, nicely undercut and hollowed out on the inside. The ends carved with faces in low relief, eyes, ears, and mouth/beak, with the reversed tail-like feature between the eyes. The corners have a small series of vertical lines on the sides, followed by a more substantial series of vertical knife cuts. Slight traces of grease.",
